# Curator PIN failure alerts
#
# The kiosk editor is gated behind a curator PIN. Each failed PIN attempt POSTs a
# JSON alert payload to the endpoint below, which is responsible for emailing
# cpkeena2@ncsu.edu.
#
# Leave this blank to disable network alerts (failed attempts are still logged to
# the browser console). To enable email delivery, point this at a relay you control
# that accepts a POST and forwards it as an email, for example:
#   - a Formspree form endpoint (https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxx)
#   - a Zapier / Make "Catch Hook" webhook wired to a Gmail/Outlook "send email" step
#   - a small serverless function (Netlify/Vercel/Cloudflare/Apps Script) using SMTP
#
# The POST body looks like:
#   { "type": "curator-pin-failure", "recipient": "cpkeena2@ncsu.edu",
#     "attemptNumber": 1, "kiosk": "Building the Wolfpack", "timestamp": "...",
#     "userAgent": "...", "page": "..." }
#
# NOTE: This value is embedded in the client bundle at build time, so only use an
# endpoint that is safe to expose publicly (no secret keys in the URL).
VITE_PIN_ALERT_ENDPOINT=

# Optional fallback curator PIN (4-8 digits) baked in at build time. Prefer setting
# the PIN per machine in public/kiosk-config.json, which is read at startup. This env
# value is only used when kiosk-config.json has no curatorPin AND the machine has no
# stored PIN yet.
VITE_CURATOR_PIN=
